  "description": "JODPID crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C52 H50 Ho4 N16 O23 1+,C2 H3 N1,N1 O3 1-,2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Ho1 (Ho) has 7 O neighbors; Ho2 (Ho) has 7 O neighbors; Ho3 (Ho) has 6 O neighbors; Ho4 (Ho) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.523-3.624 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 90.71-104.93°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C73H94N26O31Ho4. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ4-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
